ITEM P — Belgaum Station Roles & 9 km Offset Definition
-------------------------------------------------------
1. Temperature Validation Station:
   - Station ID supplying TMAX/TMIN station-days: IN009021000 (BELGAUM/SAMBRA, 15.8500°N, 74.6170°E, 747.0 m).
   - Source: run_validation.py lines 15, 34–50; audit_part2.py; data/cache/ghcn_daily/IN009021000_parsed.csv (14,718 TMAX observations).
   - IN009021100 (BELGAUM town observatory, 753.0 m) has only 1 TMAX observation in GHCN cache (data/cache/ghcn_daily/IN009021100_parsed.csv: line 2)
     and was NEVER a temperature validation station.

2. Definition of 'Endpoint' and the 9 km Offset in C.7:
   - The 9 km figure does NOT measure an offset between rainfall and temperature validation stations; both tracks used IN009021000 (Sambra airport).
   - The 9 km figure measures the distance between the originally targeted leeward transect contrast pair endpoint (Belgaum town, IN009021100, 15.8500°N, 74.5330°E)
     and the actual reporting weather station whose gauge data was ingested (Belgaum/Sambra airport, IN009021000, 15.8500°N, 74.6170°E).
   - Delta lon = 74.6170° - 74.5330° = 0.084° ≈ 9.0 km.
   - Section C.7 updated to state explicitly that IN009021000 supplied both rainfall and temperature data, while IN009021100 was solely the transect pair coordinate.


