ITEM R — DEM Provenance for Village Statistics
----------------------------------------------
Report on provenance of the headline set:
1. Originating script & log:
   - Script: run_mh_stats.py lines 121–163
   - Log: task-1947.log lines 18–58 (also task-1896.log)
2. Elevation source actually read:
   - Earth Engine cloud asset: 'USGS/SRTMGL1_003' (SRTM 1 arc-second Global) [run_mh_stats.py:121]
3. Native resolution:
   - 1 arc-second (~30 m). Coarse reanalysis projection evaluated against ECMWF/ERA5/DAILY projection (~0.25° / 28 km).
4. Polygon-mean vs point sample:
   - 16,945 village statistics (12.5% > 100m, 6.7% > 150m, p99=321m, max=610.7m): Computed via ee.Reducer.mean() across each village polygon at scale=30m (run_mh_stats.py:132). These ARE polygon means.
   - Specific named points (Amboli 590.9 m, Koynanagar 212.7 m, Radhanagari 93.4 m): Computed via ee.Reducer.first() at point coordinates (run_mh_stats.py:161). These are point samples.
5. Discrepancy with PROVENANCE.md:
   - PROVENANCE.md marked SRTM 30m as 'Not yet fetched' because no local raster files were downloaded into data/engine_cache/dem/. The computation was executed via Google Earth Engine API rather than local raster files.
   - Retraction of phrases: Relabelled Amboli 591 m as a point sample rather than a village average.


